  "problem_url": "https://www.erdosproblems.com/86",
  "description": "Spectral phase transition experiment: measure the mean level spacing ratio <r> of randomly-thinned hypercube adjacency matrices as a function of edge retention probability p. The Poisson-to-GOE crossover at <r> = 0.4407 identifies the critical p_c for each Q_n.",
  "hypothesis": "The critical edge-retention probability p_c (where <r> crosses 0.4407) decreases with n, and the C4-free constraint shifts p_c upward by suppressing spectral entropy (acting as 'entropic cooling').",
  "method": {
    "graph": "Hypercube Q_n adjacency matrix",
    "sampling": "Bernoulli edge retention with probability p",
    "observable": "Mean level spacing ratio <r> (Oganesyan-Huse)",
